[E0423] Error: a list in a constant cannot hold what owns memory
    ╭─[ err/456_lists_in_constants/main.wip:12:24 ]
    │
 12 │ val NAMES: &[String] = ["ann", "bo"]
    │                        ──────┬──────
    │                              ╰──────── `String` owns memory
    │
    │ Note: a list is kept once, where the program keeps the constant, and nothing frees what it holds
────╯
[E0304] Error: cannot assign through a `&` reference
    ╭─[ err/456_lists_in_constants/main.wip:15:5 ]
    │
 15 │     SPECS[0].keys[0] = "x"
    │     ────────┬───────
    │             ╰───────── behind a `&` reference, which only reads
    │
    │ Help: to write through it, declare the parameter `&var` and pass it with `&var`
────╯
